 			<p>“Why, Jo?” and her mother looked up quickly, as if the words suggested a double meaning.</p>
 			<p>With her eyes on her work, Jo answered soberly, “I want something new; I feel restless, and anxious to be seeing, doing, and learning more than I am. I brood too much over my own small affairs, and need stirring up, so, as I can be spared this winter, I’d like to hop a little way, and try my wings.”</p>
 			<p>“Where will you hop?”</p>
-			<p>“To New York. I had a bright idea yesterday, and this is it. You know <abbr epub:type="z3998:name-title">Mrs.</abbr> Kirke wrote to you for some respectable young person to teach her children and sew. It’s rather hard to find just the thing, but I think I should suit if I tried.”</p>
